BT /F1 10 Tf 50 800 Td 13 TL (quantity in quadrature, with each raised to the power it appears with in the formula.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Thickness h: +/- 0.02 mm on 3.00 mm, cubed: 2.0%) Tj T* (Length L: +/- 1 mm on 300 mm, cubed: 1.0%) Tj T* (Width b: +/- 0.05 mm on 25.0 mm: 0.2%) Tj T* (Gradient: +/- 0.08 mm/N from the spread between the three runs: 3.3%) Tj T* () Tj T* (Combined uncertainty: 4.0%, so E = 66.7 +/- 2.7 GPa.) Tj T* () Tj T* (The gradient and the thickness dominate. The thickness enters cubed, so a 0.02 mm error in a 3) Tj T* (mm bar matters more than a 1 mm error in its length. The clamp is the other weak point: if the) Tj T* (bar rotates slightly in the vice, the effective length is longer than 300 mm and the measured) Tj T* (deflection is too large, which would make E come out too low.) Tj T* () Tj T* (6. Discussion) Tj T* () Tj T* (The measured value of 66.7 GPa is 3.3% below the reference value of 69 GPa, and the reference) Tj T* (lies inside the uncertainty range of 64.0 to 69.4 GPa. The direction of the difference is what) Tj T* (clamp rotation would produce. The deflection-load graph is straight to within the reading) Tj T* (resolution, so the bar stayed within its elastic range up to 5.0 N, as expected: the peak) Tj T* (bending stress at 5.0 N is about 40 MPa, well below the alloy's yield strength of about 250) Tj T* (MPa.) Tj T* () Tj T* (7. Conclusion) Tj T* () Tj T* (The cantilever method gave E = 66.7 +/- 2.7 GPa for the 6082 aluminium bar, consistent with the) Tj T* (reference value of 69 GPa. The two improvements that would most reduce the uncertainty are) Tj T* (measuring the thickness with a more precise instrument at more points, and using a clamp that) Tj T* (grips the bar along a longer length to stop it rotating.) Tj T* () Tj T* ET
